    correct_option: "A",
    explanation: "Statements 1 and 2 are correct, while Statement 3 is incorrect.\nStatement 1 is correct: Paraquat (paraquat dichloride) is a bipyridylium non-selective broad-spectrum contact herbicide. When absorbed by plant chloroplasts, it intercepts electrons from Photosystem I, generating destructive reactive oxygen species (superoxide radicals) that disintegrate plant cell membranes within hours.\nStatement 2 is correct: Paraquat is notoriously toxic to mammals. It actively accumulates in pulmonary alveolar epithelial cells via polyamine transport chains, causing progressive, fatal lung fibrosis ('paraquat lung'). There is no specific medical antidote, and administering oxygen actually worsens lung toxicity by accelerating free radical generation.\nStatement 3 is incorrect: The Rotterdam Convention does NOT ban chemical manufacture or use (that is the role of the Stockholm Convention for POPs). Rotterdam merely manages the Prior Informed Consent (PIC) procedure for international trade in hazardous chemicals. Moreover, multiple parties (including India) have historically opposed listing paraquat under Annex III of the Rotterdam Convention.",
